{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.cayleyInverse_preserves_charpoly_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.cayleyInverse_preserves_charpoly_data","kind":"theorem","line":334,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L334-L363","doc":"**At `det = 1` the orientation swap preserves the whole characteristic polynomial of a\n`2×2` block, not merely its trace — so a PSD condition on such a block cannot see the swap\neither.**\n\nWhy this is needed, and it is a correction to this file's own earlier scope. The owner's\n2026-09-13 ruling on `qou-ales` (reading **(B)**, recorded on PR #7249 and in #7319) makes the\nconfinement SDP a condition on **every Wedderburn projection of the full word**, i.e. on\n`Matrix.PosSemidef` of each block. Positive-semidefiniteness is a condition on the *matrix*,\nnot on its character: in general two matrices of equal trace differ in it, so\n`trace_cayleyInverse` by itself does **not** establish that reading-3 feasibility survives the\nswap, and step 11's prose claim that \"reading-3 feasibility is a condition on the character\"\nis too strong as stated under (B).\n\nWhat rescues the conclusion is a dimension accident, and it is exactly the dimension at issue.\nFor `Fin 2` the characteristic polynomial is `λ² − (tr M)λ + (det M)`, so it is determined by\nthe pair `(tr, det)` — both of which the swap preserves at `det M = 1`. Identical\ncharacteristic polynomials force identical spectra, and a Hermitian matrix is PSD precisely\nwhen its spectrum is non-negative. The blocks the ruling names are `(2,1)` at dimension 2 and\n`(1,1,1)` at dimension 1, both `≤ 2`, so the selection survives (B) after all — by a spectral\nargument at fixed determinant, **not** because feasibility is generally a character condition.\n\nScope, stated rather than assumed: this is the `(tr, det)` half, and that half is the part\nwhich is a theorem. Passing from \"equal characteristic polynomial\" to \"equal `PosSemidef`\"\nuses the standard Hermitian spectral criterion and is **not** separately formalised here. And nothing\nabove extends to a block of dimension `≥ 3`, where `(tr, det)` no longer determine the\ncharacteristic polynomial — for those, no claim is made in either direction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.det_cayleyInverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.det_cayleyInverse","kind":"theorem","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L327-L332","doc":"**The Cayley inverse preserves the DETERMINANT as well as the trace**, and this is the\nhalf that `trace_cayleyInverse` alone does not give. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.cayleyInverse_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.cayleyInverse_eq","kind":"theorem","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L318-L325","doc":"**The `2×2` Cayley inverse in explicit form** — it is the classical adjugate: for\n`M = !![a,b;c,d]` the matrix `N = (tr M)·1 − M` is `!![d,−b;−c,a]`. Naming it explicitly is\nwhat makes the determinant below a one-line computation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.mixed_trace_not_inverse_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.mixed_trace_not_inverse_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L299-L316","doc":"**But a MIXED trace is not protected, and that is a theorem, not a measurement.** There\nexist `W`, `M`, `N` over `ℝ` with `M·N = 1` and `tr N = tr M` — so no character can tell `M`\nfrom `N` — while `tr(W·M) ≠ tr(W·N)`. Exhibited concretely:\n`W = !![1,0;0,0]`, `M = !![2,1;1,1]`, `N = !![1,-1;-1,2]`, giving traces `2` against `1`.\n\nThat is exactly the `H₆` situation. The interface bond's own character cannot see the\norientation swap (`trace_cayleyInverse`), but `tr_M(W·G³)` is a **mixed** trace against the\nnucleon word `W`, so nothing protects it — and the step-11 probe measures it flipping the\nbinding sign across the swap. The selection and the binding are guarded by different things,\nand only one of them is guarded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.trace_cayleyInverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.trace_cayleyInverse","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L289-L297","doc":"**The Cayley–Hamilton inverse of a `2×2` matrix of determinant one has the SAME trace.**\nFor `M : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) R`, Cayley–Hamilton reads `M² − (tr M)·M + (det M)·1 = 0`, so\nwhen `det M = 1` the matrix `N = (tr M)·1 − M` satisfies `M·N = 1`. Its trace is\n`2·tr M − tr M = tr M`. Step 4 proves `det V = 1` for the Hoefsmit `(2,1)` vertex image, so\nthis applies to every vertex power. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.placement_sign_not_determined_by_channel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.placement_sign_not_determined_by_channel","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L269-L281","doc":"**The sign of the binding is not determined by the channel.** Given the measured\nplacement fact, the two ratios for one channel straddle `1`, so no function of the channel\nalone fixes the sign of `B = −α·log(ratio)`. The sign is a function of the *placement*, and\nthe placement is not derived anywhere in the arc. This is the scope-(a) record: it narrows the\nreading of steps 8–10, and excludes no ingredient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.PlacementSigns.v3_below_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.PlacementSigns.v3_below_one","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L267-L267","doc":"The left-borrowing placement lowers it: the same channel comes out bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.PlacementSigns.v1_above_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.PlacementSigns.v1_above_one","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L265-L265","doc":"The right-borrowing placement raises the trace: the channel comes out unbound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.PlacementSigns.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.PlacementSigns.mk","kind":"ctor","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L263-L263","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.PlacementSigns","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.PlacementSigns","kind":"structure","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L258-L267","doc":"**The measured placement fact, carried as a hypothesis.** `ratioV1` and `ratioV3` are the\n`H₆` convention-D trace ratios of the *same* two-nucleon channel under the two straddling\nplacements. The probe measures `1.00105775…` and `0.98669973…` at the proton pin; here only\ntheir position relative to `1` is used. Verified by the probe, not proved in Lean — the same\nepistemic position as `DiprotonResponseClosedForm.ResponseClosedForm`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.no_signMixed_of_junctionFactorisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.no_signMixed_of_junctionFactorisation","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L238-L254","doc":"**The chain, end to end.** Junction factorisation ⇒ one-body ⇒ not sign-mixed. So the\nisospin pattern's failure is a *consequence* of the connected-sum structure of the two-nucleon\nclosure, not a property of the particular bond word, the particular placement, or the numbers.\n\nMeasured corroboration (step-11 probe): holding the right nucleon fixed and replacing the left\nnucleon by six unrelated words on `⟨σ₀,σ₁⟩` — including the **empty** word, a single letter, an\nall-positive word and an averaged-heavy one — leaves the response a **symbolic identity**\n`0.0139840866412832240` in every case. The response is independent of the entire left word, not\nmerely of its species, which is what this theorem predicts and what a species-only coincidence\nwould not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.response_oneBody_of_junctionFactorisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.response_oneBody_of_junctionFactorisation","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L205-L236","doc":"**From junction factorisation to one-body.** The reason the response is one-body is not a\ncoincidence about nucleon species. `W₁` lies in the parabolic `⟨σ₀,σ₁⟩` (strands 1–3) while\n`W₂` *and a right-borrowing bond* both lie in `⟨σ₂,σ₃,σ₄⟩` (strands 3–6); the two strand sets\n**overlap in one strand**, so the closure is a connected sum and the Markov trace is\nmultiplicative across it. Both traces then carry the same left factor, which cancels:\n\n    f a b = (tL a · tR^bond b) / (tL a · tR⁰ b) = tR^bond b / tR⁰ b.\n\nStated here abstractly, so it applies at either placement by swapping the roles.\n\nThe premise is the standard multiplicativity of a link invariant under connected sum, which\n`mass-theory/canonical-trace-factorises-over-chain.md` states and relies on — *\"a closed braid\nwhose word is a product of sub-words on strand sets overlapping in one strand is a connected\nsum, and the Markov trace … is multiplicative under connected sum\"* — and which that block's\nown §Status records as **not formalised**. So this file derives the one-body property *from* a\ncited principle rather than asserting it from a table; the principle itself remains unproved\nhere, which is why nothing below is scope-(b).\n\n**Do not read this as `MarkovTraceMultiplicative`.** That models the **disjoint union**, and\nbean `qou-bsfg` exists because the two were once conflated. The *free* two-nucleon trace is a\ndisjoint union (supports `{0,1}` and `{3,4}` share no strand); the *bonded* one is a connected\nsum (the bond reaches across strand 3). Different properties. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.signMixed_is_genuinely_two_body","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.signMixed_is_genuinely_two_body","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L192-L201","doc":"**The contrapositive, as the positive statement of what a closure needs**: any pair\nfunctional realising the isospin pattern is genuinely two-body — it depends on both arguments.\nThis is what step 11 hands forward as the requirement, rather than a refutation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.no_signMixed_of_oneBody","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.no_signMixed_of_oneBody","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L180-L190","doc":"**Either way, and this is the headline.** Every interface placement borrows from exactly\none side (`interfaceVertex_borrows_exactly_one_side`), and the response is measured to be a\nfunction of that borrowed nucleon alone at **all four** vertices. So no placement of a γγ\nvertex at this interface — either position, either orientation — can carry the two-body isospin\npattern. The obstruction is the *arity* of the response, not the sign of any number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.no_signMixed_of_leftDependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.no_signMixed_of_leftDependent","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L171-L178","doc":"**The mirror**: a response depending only on its LEFT argument cannot be sign-mixed\neither, via `f p n = g p = f p p`. This is the measured situation at `V3` and `V4`, which\nborrow from the left. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.no_signMixed_of_rightDependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.no_signMixed_of_rightDependent","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L161-L169","doc":"**A response that depends only on its RIGHT argument cannot be sign-mixed.** This is the\nmeasured situation at `V1` **and `V2`**: `r_pp = r_np` and `r_nn = r_pn`, so `r` is `g` of the\nborrowed (right) nucleon. Then `f p n = g n = f n n`, and a real times itself is never\nnegative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.SignMixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.SignMixed","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L155-L159","doc":"**The two-body isospin pattern** bean `qou-q8vl` requires of a pair functional: the unlike\npair sits on the opposite side of zero from **both** like pairs. Stated on products so it is\nsign-agnostic — it says \"opposite sign\", not \"positive\" or \"negative\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.instDecidableEqNucleon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.instDecidableEqNucleon","kind":"instance","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L153-L153","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.Nucleon.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.Nucleon.n","kind":"ctor","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L152-L152","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.Nucleon.p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.Nucleon.p","kind":"ctor","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L151-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.Nucleon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.Nucleon","kind":"inductive","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L149-L153","doc":"A nucleon species. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.interfaceVertex_borrows_exactly_one_side","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.interfaceVertex_borrows_exactly_one_side","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L137-L145","doc":"**A straddling vertex borrows from exactly one nucleon.** `g = 1` meets the left support\nand misses the right; `g = 2` meets the right and misses the left. Never both, never neither —\nso every placement breaks the pair's left–right symmetry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.straddles_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.straddles_iff","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L131-L135","doc":"**Exactly two placements straddle the interface**, `g = 1` and `g = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.no_vertex_on_interface_alone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.no_vertex_on_interface_alone","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L121-L129","doc":"**A vertex support is never the interface alone.** It has two distinct elements, so it\ncannot equal the singleton `{2}` — there is no symmetric placement to prefer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.supports_disjoint_and_miss_interface","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.supports_disjoint_and_miss_interface","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L115-L119","doc":"The two nucleon supports are disjoint, and neither contains the interface generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.Straddles","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.Straddles","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L112-L113","doc":"A vertex **straddles** the interface when its support contains the interface generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.vertexSupport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.vertexSupport","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L109-L110","doc":"The generator pair a γγ vertex `σ_g σ_{g+1}⁻¹` occupies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.interfaceGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.interfaceGen","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L106-L107","doc":"The interface generator, the one belonging to neither nucleon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.rightSupport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.rightSupport","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L103-L104","doc":"The generator support of the right nucleon in `H₆`: `{3, 4}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.leftSupport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.InterfaceVertexArity.leftSupport","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/InterfaceVertexArity.lean#L100-L101","doc":"The generator support of the left nucleon in `H₆`: `{0, 1}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}